@startuml LLM_Application_Lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3E5F5
  BorderColor #7B1FA2
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #263238
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  DiamondBorderColor #F57F17
}

title End-to-End LLM Application Lifecycle (Using Pre-trained Models)

start

:**1. Application Planning**
----
* Define use case
  (Chatbot, Summarization, Q&A,
   Content Generation, Translation)
* Identify target users
* Define success metrics
* Set performance requirements
  (Latency, Accuracy, Cost)
* Determine scale requirements
* Budget planning
* Choose deployment model
  (Cloud API, Self-hosted, Hybrid);

:**2. LLM Provider Selection**
----
* Research available models:
  - OpenAI (GPT-4, GPT-3.5)
  - Anthropic (Claude)
  - Google (Gemini, PaLM)
  - Meta (Llama)
  - Mistral, Cohere, etc.
* Compare model capabilities
* Evaluate pricing models
* Check API rate limits
* Assess latency requirements
* Review terms of service
* Consider data privacy
* Test model quality;

:**3. API Integration Setup**
----
* Obtain API keys/credentials
* Set up authentication
* Configure SDK/libraries
* Set up development environment
* Configure network settings
* Set up SSL/TLS
* Configure timeouts
* Set up retry mechanisms
* Implement rate limiting
* Configure connection pooling;

:**4. Input Text Preparation**
----
* Receive user input
* Validate input format
* Check input length
* Sanitize input text:
  - Remove malicious content
  - Strip unwanted characters
  - Normalize whitespace
* Apply content filtering
* Detect language
* Check for PII (Personal Info)
* Log input (if allowed)
* Prepare input metadata;

:**5. Prompt Engineering**
----
* Design prompt templates
* Add system instructions
* Include context/examples
  (Few-shot learning)
* Structure input format
* Add role definitions
* Include constraints/rules
* Format output requirements
* Add guardrails
* Optimize prompt length
* Version prompt templates
* A/B test prompts;

:**6. Context Management**
----
* Retrieve conversation history
* Maintain session state
* Manage context window
  (e.g., 4K, 8K, 32K tokens)
* Implement context truncation
* Prioritize relevant context
* Add metadata
* Handle multi-turn dialogue
* Store user preferences
* Manage system context;

:**7. Token Estimation**
----
* Count input tokens
* Estimate prompt tokens
* Calculate context tokens
* Estimate output tokens
* Total token calculation
* Check against limits
* Estimate API cost
* Validate token budget
* Adjust if needed;

if (Token Limit\nExceeded?) then (Yes)
  :**Handle Token Overflow**
  ----
  * Truncate context
  * Summarize history
  * Remove low-priority content
  * Split into chunks
  * Use compression techniques;
  
else (No)
endif

:**8. Request Configuration**
----
* Set model parameters:
  - Temperature (0.0-2.0)
  - Top-p (nucleus sampling)
  - Top-k sampling
  - Max tokens (output limit)
  - Frequency penalty
  - Presence penalty
  - Stop sequences
* Configure streaming (if needed)
* Set timeout values
* Add request metadata
* Configure response format;

:**9. API Request Execution**
----
* Construct API payload
* Add headers and auth
* Send HTTP/gRPC request
* Handle streaming (if enabled)
* Monitor request status
* Implement retry logic
  (Exponential backoff)
* Handle rate limiting
  (429 errors)
* Track request latency
* Log API calls;

if (Request\nSuccessful?) then (Yes)
else (No)
  :**Error Handling**
  ----
  * Classify error type:
    - Network error
    - Timeout
    - Rate limit (429)
    - Authentication (401)
    - Server error (500)
    - Invalid request (400)
  * Implement retry strategy
  * Use fallback model
  * Return cached response
  * User-friendly error message
  * Log error details;
  
  if (Retry\nAttempt?) then (Yes)
    :Wait and Retry;
    detach
  else (No)
    :Return Error Response;
    stop
  endif
endif

:**10. Response Reception**
----
* Receive API response
* Validate response format
* Extract generated text
* Capture token usage:
  - Prompt tokens
  - Completion tokens
  - Total tokens
* Record response time
* Extract metadata
* Handle streaming chunks
  (if streaming enabled)
* Validate completeness;

:**11. Token Conversion & Processing**
----
* Decode token IDs to text
  (handled by API)
* Receive natural language output
* Understand token breakdown
* Verify output format
* Check for completion
* Detect truncation
  (if max_tokens reached)
* Log token metrics;

:**12. Output Post-Processing**
----
* Extract final text
* Remove artifacts
* Format output:
  - Parse JSON/XML
  - Extract code blocks
  - Format markdown
* Apply text cleanup
* Remove unwanted content
* Validate output quality
* Check for hallucinations
* Apply content filtering
* Sanitize output;

:**13. Content Moderation**
----
* Check for inappropriate content
* Detect harmful outputs
* Filter toxic language
* Verify factual accuracy
  (if critical)
* Check for PII leakage
* Validate safety guidelines
* Apply business rules
* Flag suspicious content
* Log moderation results;

if (Content\nSafe?) then (No)
  :**Handle Unsafe Content**
  ----
  * Block output
  * Log incident
  * Return safe alternative
  * Notify administrators
  * Update filters;
  
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**14. Caching Strategy**
----
* Check cache for similar queries
* Generate cache keys
  (hash of input)
* Store responses in cache:
  - Redis
  - Memcached
  - CDN
* Set TTL (Time To Live)
* Implement cache invalidation
* Use semantic caching
* Balance freshness vs. cost
* Monitor cache hit rate;

:**15. Response Delivery**
----
* Format final response
* Add metadata
* Prepare response payload
* Send to client/user
* Track delivery status
* Implement real-time updates
  (for streaming)
* Handle client errors
* Confirm delivery;

:**16. Usage Tracking & Logging**
----
* Log API usage:
  - Request count
  - Token consumption
  - Cost per request
  - Response time
* Track user interactions
* Store conversation history
  (if permitted)
* Log errors and warnings
* Track model performance
* Monitor API quotas
* Generate usage reports
* Update billing metrics;

:**17. Cost Management**
----
* Calculate request cost
* Track daily/monthly spending
* Monitor token usage patterns
* Identify cost optimization:
  - Use smaller models
  - Optimize prompts
  - Implement caching
  - Batch requests
* Set budget alerts
* Track ROI
* Optimize model selection
* Review pricing tiers;

:**18. Performance Monitoring**
----
* Track response latency:
  - API latency
  - Total request time
  - Time-to-first-token
* Monitor throughput
* Track success/error rates
* Measure availability
* Monitor API health
* Track model version
* Detect degradation
* Set up alerting;

:**19. Quality Assessment**
----
* Collect user feedback:
  - Thumbs up/down
  - Ratings
  - Comments
* Evaluate output quality
* Measure accuracy
* Track hallucinations
* Assess relevance
* Monitor user satisfaction
* Analyze edge cases
* Compare against benchmarks
* Generate quality reports;

:**20. User Feedback Collection**
----
* Implement feedback UI
* Collect explicit feedback
* Track implicit signals:
  - Session duration
  - Retry rates
  - Edit rates
* Gather feature requests
* Identify pain points
* Store feedback data
* Analyze feedback trends
* Prioritize improvements;

:**21. Prompt Optimization**
----
* Analyze poorly performing prompts
* Test prompt variations
* A/B test different templates
* Optimize prompt length
* Improve instruction clarity
* Add better examples
* Refine output format
* Update system messages
* Version control prompts
* Document best practices;

:**22. Model Version Management**
----
* Track model versions used
* Monitor model updates
  from provider
* Test new model versions
* Compare performance
* Gradual migration strategy
* Maintain compatibility
* Handle deprecations
* Update API endpoints
* Document version changes;

:**23. Security & Compliance**
----
* Implement access control
* Encrypt API keys
* Rotate credentials
* Audit API usage
* Monitor for abuse
* Ensure GDPR compliance
* Handle data retention
* Implement privacy controls
* Log security events
* Regular security reviews;

:**24. Scaling & Optimization**
----
* Implement load balancing
* Use request queuing
* Batch similar requests
* Implement async processing
* Scale infrastructure
* Optimize concurrent requests
* Use multiple API keys
* Distribute across regions
* Handle traffic spikes
* Monitor resource usage;

if (Performance\nIssues?) then (Yes)
  :**Troubleshoot & Optimize**
  ----
  * Identify bottlenecks
  * Optimize API calls
  * Improve caching
  * Adjust rate limits
  * Scale infrastructure
  * Switch model/provider
  * Optimize prompts
  * Review architecture;
  
else (No)
endif

:**25. Continuous Improvement**
----
* Analyze usage patterns
* Review cost efficiency
* Update prompt library
* Improve error handling
* Enhance caching strategy
* Optimize token usage
* Refine content moderation
* Update monitoring dashboards
* Iterate on features
* Plan roadmap;

if (Major Issues\nDetected?) then (Yes)
  :Review & Redesign\nProcess;
  note right
    Revisit: Planning,
    Provider Selection,
    Architecture Design
  end note
else (No)
  :Maintain Operations;
endif

stop

legend right
  |= **LLM Application Phases** |
  | **Phase 1: Setup** |
  | - Application Planning |
  | - Provider Selection |
  | - API Integration |
  | **Phase 2: Request Processing** |
  | - Input Preparation |
  | - Prompt Engineering |
  | - Context Management |
  | - Token Estimation |
  | **Phase 3: API Interaction** |
  | - Request Configuration |
  | - API Request Execution |
  | - Error Handling |
  | **Phase 4: Response Handling** |
  | - Response Reception |
  | - Token Processing |
  | - Output Post-Processing |
  | - Content Moderation |
  | **Phase 5: Delivery** |
  | - Caching |
  | - Response Delivery |
  | **Phase 6: Operations** |
  | - Usage Tracking |
  | - Cost Management |
  | - Performance Monitoring |
  | - Quality Assessment |
  | **Phase 7: Optimization** |
  | - User Feedback |
  | - Prompt Optimization |
  | - Model Version Mgmt |
  | - Security & Compliance |
  | - Scaling |
  | - Continuous Improvement |
endlegend

note right
  **Key Concepts:**
  * Using pre-trained LLMs via API
  * Text → Tokens (handled by API)
  * Token counting & estimation
  * Cost optimization critical
  * Prompt engineering essential
  * Caching for efficiency
  * Monitoring & observability
  * User feedback loop
  
  **Important Metrics:**
  * Token usage (input/output)
  * API latency
  * Cost per request
  * Cache hit rate
  * Error rates
  * User satisfaction
  * Quality scores
end note

@enduml
